<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>8.9.1: Finding a Solution through Substitution</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02231</md:content-id>
    <md:title>8.9.1: Finding a Solution through Substitution</md:title>
    <md:uuid>70a6bc37-bcc7-47fc-aa53-b7f070f4bca1</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Let's try to find at least one solution to \(x^2− 2x − 35 = 0\).</para>
<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<example><exercise>
  <problem>
    
    <para>Create a table of values. In column 1, enter the whole numbers between 0 and 10 to represent values of x. In column 2, evaluate the expression \(x^2-2x-35\) using the values for \(x\).
      </para>
    <para>Write down your answers, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
  </problem><solution>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
  <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable">
    <thead/>
    <tbody>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
          \(x\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          0
        </entry>
        <entry>
          1
        </entry>
        <entry>
          2
        </entry>
        <entry>
          3
        </entry>
        <entry>
          4
        </entry>
        <entry>
          5
        </entry>
        <entry>
          6
        </entry>
        <entry>
          7
        </entry>
        <entry>
          8
        </entry>
        <entry>
          9
        </entry>
        <entry>
          10
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry scope="row" class="emphasis">
          \(x^2-2x -35\)
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –35
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –36
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –35
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –32
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –27
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –20
        </entry>
        <entry>
          –11
        </entry>
        <entry>
          0
        </entry>
        <entry>
          13
        </entry>
        <entry>
          28
        </entry>
        <entry>
          45
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
  <para>We can see from the table that a solution to the equation is \(x = 7\) since \(x^2- 2x - 35 = 0\) at that value.</para>
</solution></exercise>
</example><!--Interaction End -->

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
    <para>There is another number outside of 0 to 10 that would make the expression \(x^2− 2x − 35\) equal 0. Can you find it?</para>
    </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter the number outside of 0 to 10 that would make the expression \(x^2− 2x − 35\) equal 0.</para>
  <para>Compare your answer:</para>
    <para>The other zero for the equation is located at \(x=-5\), but it is possible that you did not consider negative numbers.</para>
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End -->
</section>
</content>
